# gitleaks fingerprints that are known false positives.
#
# One line per finding, in the format gitleaks itself prints:
#
#     <commit>:<file>:<rule-id>:<line>
#
# The entry below is the token-shaped literal the Phase 8-9 test suite used to
# prove LogSanitizer redacts GitHub tokens. Commit 24fa86b replaced every such
# fixture in the working tree with an obvious placeholder, but a history scan
# reads the commits, not the tree, and a history scan is the whole point of the
# "Secrets" job: "we deleted it" and "it was never there" are different claims.
#
# The value is allow-listed by fingerprint rather than by file or by rule, so
# the rule stays armed for the rest of that file and for every future commit.
